  "details": "I've had to use the group blocking feature recently for a few group public lobbies I joined where the group admins were not very welcoming, so to prevent myself from being able to join their public lobbies again by accident, I blocked their groups. Several other friends had also told me they had experienced similar things with group publics and had blocked other groups as well for the similar reasons, so I thought I'd look into how group blocking works because in this case where we don't want to join their lobbies by accident again it actually seems like it would be useful.\n\nWhen you block a group, it comes up with this message:\n\n\"You've Blocked this Group!\n\nYou won't get any invites from this group, and you can't join it.\n\nIf you want to join this group or get invites from it, you have to unblock it first.\"\n\nHowever, after doing a test to see how it works, while you can't recieve invites from or join the group itself on the website, I found you can _still join group public lobbies_ that are being hosted by a group you've blocked (and presumably this would be the same with group+ lobbies as well etc). \n\nI think it would be more beneficial if it excluded their group public or group+ lobbies from your worlds list or prevented you from joining it with a message such as \"You can't join this instance because you have blocked the group that is hosting it\" or something of the sort. That way the group block feature will be much more powerful and useful.",
